# Moni – Project Overview

**Moni** is a local-first, privacy-focused personal finance app: wallets, transactions, analytics, and AI that turns natural language, receipt photos, and (Android) bank notifications into transactions: the first of a kind becomes a **reviewable proposal** (`proposed_transactions` + a review UI); routine bank notifications matching the user's own categorized history are added directly and marked auto-added (`lib/ai/routine.ts`).

## Monorepo (Turborepo + pnpm)

```
apps/mobile/      Expo SDK 57 + expo-router — PRIMARY client (focus)
apps/backend/     Go + Gin AI gateway → OpenRouter (focus)
apps/web/         Next.js 16 dashboard — ISOLATED, deprioritized
packages/types/   @repo/types — Zod schemas + inferred TS types
supabase/         Migrations, RLS, storage
docs/             ARCHITECTURE / SETUP / DATABASE / AI / research
```

Run: `pnpm --filter moni dev` / `pnpm --filter backend dev` / `pnpm --filter web dev`. Go integrates with turbo via package.json scripts (`go run` / `go vet` / `go test`).

## Architecture rules

- **Mobile syncs directly to Supabase** via Legend-State (`apps/mobile/lib/store/index.ts`) with MMKV persistence and soft deletes. There is NO PowerSync, NO SQLite/Drizzle, NO local LLM — do not reintroduce them.
- **Mobile and web never talk to each other.** Web's API routes serve only the web dashboard. Shared needs go through Supabase (data) or the Go backend (AI).
- **Go backend is stateless**: verifies Supabase user JWTs via JWKS (ES256), calls OpenRouter, returns extractions. No database access.
- **Supabase keys**: new system only — `sb_publishable_...` in clients, `sb_secret_...` server-side. Never use legacy anon/service_role keys.
- **AI wire contract**: `apps/mobile/lib/ai/client/types.ts` ↔ `apps/backend/internal/extract/types.go` must stay in sync manually.

## Conventions

- TypeScript strict; all shared shapes as Zod schemas in `@repo/types`, types inferred — never duplicated
- Auth: Supabase JWT Bearer tokens; ES256 asymmetric signing
- Error responses: `{ error: string; details?: any }`
- Money: `DECIMAL(12,2)`, 3-letter ISO currency; UUID primary keys
- Designed for ~1000 users at minimal cost (Supabase free tier, OpenRouter pay-per-token, Cloud Run scale-to-zero)

## Redesign v2

The mobile app is being rebuilt to a new design kept on a claude.ai design canvas. Before building or changing any mobile screen, read `docs/REDESIGN.md`: which canvas boards to build and which to ignore, the target navigation (Home · Activity · + · Budget · Debts; Moni chat as a pushed page), the rules every screen follows, the code gaps, and the open owner decisions. Values and words: `docs/redesign/tokens.md`, `docs/redesign/glossary.md`.

## Product research

Before you plan features, pricing, onboarding, or AI behavior, read `docs/research/competitor-reviews-2026-10.md`. It summarizes about 30k competitor app-store reviews and research on the Malaysian market (October 2026), and states what they imply for Moni.
